==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|proficiens|lang=la}}, present participle of {{term|proficere|lang=la||to go forward, advance, make progress, succeed, be profitable or useful}} < {{term|pro||forth, forward}} + {{term|facere||to make, do}}; see [[fact]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/pɹəˈfɪʃ.ənt/}}, {{SAMPA|/pr@"fIS.@nt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-proficient.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Good at; [[skilled]]; [[fluent]]; [[practiced]], especially in relation to a task or skill.
#: ''He was a '''proficient''' writer with an interest in human nature.''

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|good at}} [[skilled]], [[fluent]], [[practiced]]

